sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2023-competency-14> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "The authors suggest that intelligence, understood as problem-solving competency, was an evolutionary driver long before complex brains and muscle-driven behaviour arose, so basal cognition is an important part of evolutionary developmental biology.";
    dc:type "historical-inference";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Problem-solving competency drove evolution long before brains";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Shreesha L, Levin M, “Cellular Competency during Development Alters Evolutionary Dynamics in an Artificial Embryogeny Model”, Entropy (Basel, Switzerland) (2023), doi:10.3390/e25010131; section “5. Conclusions”. Scope: Evolution of life before nervous systems"
}
